# The Body after a ParameterGuard relies on what the guard tested. Only the build's verifier checked a call of the Body against that.
# With the proof-checking switches the Body took `tested` as proven, and with CheckProofsAtEntries it was not checked at all, because the fused entry comes before the guard.
# Fault injection, testing=UnderstateEffects:Callee/f1/TestsOfGuard: the emitter lets every test of the guard of f1 pass. The walk, the verifier of calls and Validate see a correct guard.
# Two strings in boxes of `undefined|number` compare equal.
# f1 = same
# RUN: plan units mechanisms=all
# CHECK: unit f1:ParameterGuard (JSValue, JSValue) -> (JSValue) tests (undefined|number, undefined|number)
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# RIGHT: 3 -1
# RIGHT-NEXT: 0
# RIGHT-NEXT: went on
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(LIE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=UnderstateEffects:Callee/f1/TestsOfGuard
# LIE: 3 -1
# LIE-NEXT: 3
# LIE-NEXT: went on
# RUN(ENTRIES): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtEntries,UnderstateEffects:Callee/f1/TestsOfGuard
# ENTRIES: 3 -1
# ENTRIES: found string in an argument
# ENTRIES-NOT: went on
# ENTRIES: crashed
# RUN(PROOFS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,UnderstateEffects:Callee/f1/TestsOfGuard
# PROOFS: 3 -1
# PROOFS: found string in an argument
# PROOFS-NOT: went on
# PROOFS: crashed
